From 3712b7b250e3452e5b1142aca6e7a6cc13353c87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:51:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: run the suite on Qt 4.8

QSignalSpy and connect() sites use the SIGNAL()/SLOT() string form, the one
lambda slot became a member slot, qOverload<> disambiguations became explicit
signatures, and Qt5-only calls (QByteArrayLiteral, toSecsSinceEpoch, cbegin,
QUrl::FullyDecoded, QSignalSpy::wait, QWidget::grab, emitting another
object's signal) got all-version forms or guarded fallbacks. The locale test
gains the same Qt4 lrelease recipe and locale.qrc as src/. Nothing is
excluded: all 24 test binaries pass on Qt 4.8.7 (Xvfb) and the sources still
build unchanged on Qt 5.15/6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SNLMjDKKUDw5GKpBW96KSN
